{
  "id": "Compound::DB01601 - Gene::5243",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Lopinavir may interact with Abcb1 through a series of molecular pathways involving cytochrome P450 enzymes. Specifically, Lopinavir binds to Cyp2d6 and Cyp2b6, which are involved in the metabolism of codeine and morphine, and also in the metabolism of amprenavir, respectively. These enzymes are known to be regulated by the Abcb1 gene, which encodes a transporter involved in the efflux of drugs from cells. The interaction between Lopinavir and Abcb1 is thus indirectly supported through the metabolic pathways of other compounds that bind to the same enzymes. The varying scores in the different paths reflect the strength of these interactions, with higher scores indicating stronger relationships. The evidence suggests that Lopinavir may influence Abcb1 through its effects on the metabolic processes of other drugs, highlighting a complex network of drug-target interactions.",
